  "name": "it-reelsmaker",
  "description": "Edit vertical short videos (Reels, Shorts, TikTok) from talking-head, two-person or horizontal footage, cut a long recording (podcast, webinar, interview) into clips, lay voice notes over your own shots, or make a video with no footage: a brand promo, or designed scenes over a voice note from your phone, optionally with a brand mascot drawn in code. Local transcription, pauses and retakes cut by audio, virtual camera and on-brand motion graphics in Remotion, word-timed subtitles and their translation, optional inserts (B-roll, code scenes, memes), face-aware layout, −14 LUFS mastering, 1080×1920 render. Use when asked to edit, cut or fix a vertical video: “edit a reel”, “make a Reel from IMG_xxxx.MOV”, “clips from this podcast”, “add subtitles / a hook / a cover / B-roll”, “translate the subtitles”, “a promo without footage”, “a video from my voice note”, “add a mascot”, “the video jumps back”. Not for long horizontal edits, format conversion or compression. Needs ffmpeg, Node.js with Remotion and Python.",
